# A conversation lost is kept on the tree as one won is, and says so: the node under the act that
# opened it reads "failure", in the ink of a loss, with the replies that led there. He is named in
# it all the same: a conversation lost is still a meeting.
#
# The mirror of dialogue_record.cli — same tree, same branch, opposite roll.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Reach the conversation through the verb that opens it.
strategy succeed
goal meet_stranger
advance 12 180
click observe "brewer"
choose childhood_memory
advance 12 180
click think "brewer"
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click act 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
wait mode Dialogue 60

# The verb had to succeed for there to be a conversation; the roll under test is the resolution's.
strategy fail-dice
advance 20 180
click option 0
advance 20 180
click option 0
advance 20 180
click continue
advance 20 180
expect Then keep walking

click button
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

expect-state trees dialogue with=brewer ending=failure replies=2
point dialogue last
wait
expect-state pointer-label ground=grey text=talked with Aeemilyus · failure
expect CONVERSATION WITH AEEMILYUS
expect it came to: failure
quit
